# Caddyfile — reverse proxy with a self-signed (locally-trusted) certificate.
# Caddy generates and manages its own local CA automatically ("tls internal"),
# so no manual openssl commands are needed. You just need to trust that CA's
# root certificate once on this same machine (see CLAUDE_DESKTOP_LOCAL_SETUP.md
# / the steps Claude gave you in chat).
#
# Same-machine setup: Claude Desktop and the MCP server are both on this box,
# so the site address is just "localhost".
{
	# Global options block intentionally left empty — defaults are fine.
}

https://localhost {
	tls internal

	# Proxies to the wazuh-main-server container over the internal Docker
	# network — this works whether or not the server's own port is published
	# to the host, since Compose puts every service in this project on the
	# same default network.
	reverse_proxy wazuh-main-server:3000
}
